{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "For U1, leverage the existing Hortonworks Teradata connector pattern (TeradataConnManager) rather than building a custom JDBC bridge; treat the NPE as a missing default connection-manager resolution in Sqoop's job launcher.",
    "For U2, externalize the logging directory through Spring's property placeholder mechanism (e.g., xd.logging.dir) with a fallback to ${xd.home}/logs to preserve backward compatibility.",
    "For U3, create spring-bus as a new top-level Maven multi-module project; move message-bus code preserving the public API and use Maven dependency inheritance to consume it from Spring XD.",
    "For U4, move the type-conversion service abstractions (Converter, ConversionService wiring) into spring-cloud-dataflow core, exposing a stable SPI that custom modules can implement.",
    "For U5, place the serialization codec in spring-bus alongside message-bus, with a pluggable CodecStrategy interface (Jackson, Kryo, etc.) so XD can inherit via dependency.",
    "For U6, implement the singlenode Admin SPI on top of an in-JVM ModuleLauncher that uses local message channels and an embedded servlet/runtime, suitable for local developer workflows.",
    "For U7, implement the Diego Receptor Admin SPI as a remote ModuleLauncher client using the Receptor/BBS API; modules are submitted as Diego LRPs and registered with the XD message bus.",
    "For U8, evaluate Eureka and Consul as candidate service-discovery backends; produce a small POC and design notes rather than a full production implementation."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Each work day is 8 productive hours (no meeting overhead deducted).",
    "The Spring XD, spring-bus (new), and spring-cloud-dataflow source trees already exist locally and build successfully with Maven before work begins.",
    "A single senior developer performs all work end-to-end, so no hand-off overhead is included beyond normal code review/rework already folded into each activity.",
    "Unit tests and integration tests are part of each activity's effort; no separate QA cycle is added.",
    "Java 8 (or 17+ for newer Spring) and the necessary Hortonworks/Teradata, Diego, and Cloud Foundry tooling are available locally or in CI.",
    "Diego Receptor API and CF Lattice are stable and accessible; no platform-team coordination delays are accounted for.",
    "Documentation is limited to release notes and short design notes; no full user-guide or admin-guide rewrite is in scope.",
    "No major architectural surprises or cross-team blockers are encountered during execution."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Teradata Sqoop integration (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Reproduce the NPE when using the Teradata JDBC driver directly, register org.apache.sqoop.teradata.TeradataConnManager as a known connection-manager (or install the Hortonworks connector), wire it into the Sqoop job launcher, and add integration tests covering import jobs against a Teradata instance.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Configurable logging directory (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Introduce an xd.logging.dir (or equivalent) property, plumb it through the logging subsystem (e.g., log4j/logback file appender configuration) with a default of ${xd.home}/logs, and update the RPM/deployment script defaults to point at /var/log/spring-xd.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Move message-bus into spring-bus (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Create the new spring-bus Maven module(s), relocate the message-bus source code and tests, ensure public API and Spring configuration metadata are preserved, update Spring XD's pom.xml to depend on spring-bus, and verify all existing tests and stream scenarios pass.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Move type conversion into spring-cloud-dataflow (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Extract input/output type-conversion classes and related SPI into spring-cloud-dataflow, expose a stable module-facing conversion service so custom modules can produce/consume custom domain objects, update Spring XD imports, and re-run module registration/composition tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Move serialization codec into spring-bus (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Relocate the serialization codec implementation(s) into spring-bus behind a CodecStrategy abstraction, ensure it composes cleanly with the relocated message-bus, and re-wire Spring XD to depend on the new module while validating bus round-trip behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Singlenode XD Admin SPI implementation (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement an in-JVM XD Admin SPI backed by a local ModuleLauncher. Use embedded message channels and an embedded container so streams/tasks can be orchestrated locally without an external runtime; provide a launcher entry point and integration tests for representative stream and job modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Diego Receptor XD Admin SPI implementation (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a Diego Receptor-based ModuleLauncher that submits modules as Diego LRPs and tracks their lifecycle, wire it into the XD Admin SPI for CF Lattice/Diego deployments, handle secure Receptor/BBS communication, and test end-to-end stream execution on a Diego environment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "s-c-s service discovery self-registration investigation (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Investigate how spring-cloud-stream modules could self-register with a service-discovery backend, evaluate Eureka and Consul as candidates, build a small proof-of-concept demonstrating discovery and orchestration by the XD runtime on CF, and produce a short design note with recommendations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Cross-feature integration and regression testing",
      "activity_description": "Run a full integration pass covering all U1–U8 changes together: end-to-end stream/job execution on the singlenode and Diego launchers, Teradata import via Sqoop, configurable logging, and the new message-bus / type-conversion / codec wiring. Fix any regressions uncovered.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Release notes and design documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write concise release notes summarizing the new Teradata support, configurable logging, the spring-bus / spring-cloud-dataflow moves, the new Admin SPI implementations, and the service-discovery findings; update relevant reference docs and changelogs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 53
  }
}
```

